The requirement-ID coverage check (`spec.md` uses key `CPN`) passes on presence: all three IDs — CPN-1, CPN-2, CPN-3 — have a matching tagged test in `tests/checkout.test.ts`, no untested/undefined/unlabeled gaps.

The Judgement pass (which checks whether tagged tests actually assert what they claim) is skipped — `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` isn't set. But reading the file directly turns up one real problem:

**`CPN-3: rejects an over-limit coupon` (tests/checkout.test.ts:11-13) has no assertion.**
```ts
it('CPN-3: rejects an over-limit coupon', () => {
  applyCoupon(cart, usedUpCoupon);
});
```
It calls `applyCoupon` but never checks the result — it'll pass even if the coupon is wrongly accepted. Needs an `expect(res.ok).toBe(false)` (or similar) before review, otherwise CPN-3 is untested in practice despite passing the presence check.

CPN-1 and CPN-2 both assert correctly and look fine.

